      "timestamp": "2026-08-30T22:29:25.298518+00:00",
      "type": "understanding",
      "summary": "Agent explained goal and mechanics.",
      "understanding": {
        "goal_understanding": "Navigate the grid to complete each level by stepping onto every goal cell while carrying a piece whose shape, color, and rotation exactly match that goal\u2019s required attributes; once all goals in a level are completed you advance, and losing all lives ends the game.",
        "mechanics_understanding": "Each move (north/south/east/west) costs 1 stamina; when stamina reaches 0 you lose 1 life and stamina resets to max, and if lives hit 0 it\u2019s GAME_OVER. Walls block movement and the state provides blocked_directions, which should never be chosen because attempting them wastes a turn and stamina without moving. Modifier tiles change the carried piece: shape modifiers cycle shapes 0\u20135 (wrap), color modifiers cycle orange\u2192blue\u2192green\u2192red\u2192orange (wrap), and rotation modifiers rotate 90\u00b0 clockwise through 0\u00b0\u219290\u00b0\u2192180\u00b0\u2192270\u00b0\u21920\u00b0 (wrap). A goal only activates when shape, color, and rotation all match simultaneously, and stepping onto an activated goal completes it; careful routing avoids blocked directions and minimizes wasted stamina."
      }
    }
